  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1225 AM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nThe main trough axis located across the Desert Southwest remains \nforecast to eject well to the northeast early week but trailing \nshortwave energy would still enter our region from late Monday \nthrough Tuesday. The medium range guidance has continued to back \naway from any semblance of a cold front approaching the region \nthrough early week. However, the shortwave does allow for the \narrival of some moisture aloft and this looks to perhaps combine \nwith the low level moisture with the onshore flow to squeeze out \nsome light rain chances (15-30%) from late Monday night into \nTuesday. Rain chances look to mainly decline from Wednesday into \nearly Thursday but a couple of spotty showers into the Coastal \nPlains may still remain possible. Expect mild temperatures along \nwith humid conditions to continue with the southeasterly flow.\n\nThere is considerable spread in the guidance near the end of the \nforecast period and towards the start of the Halloween weekend. \nHowever, there remains some signal within the ensembles and \nperiodically individually from the deterministic/AI guidance for \nincreasing rain potential with connections from off the Eastern \nPacific in association with Tropical Storm Vance.",
